<span class=\"gk\">σελήνιον</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">11</span> </span>. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"2\"><span class=\"lex-n\">II</span> as fem. pr. n., <b class=\"lex-tr\">Selene, the goddess of the moon</b> (never in <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Hom.</span> </span>), <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Hes.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Th.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">371</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">h.Merc.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">100</span> </span>, etc. (<span class=\"gk\">σελήνη </span>(<span class=\"lex-etym gk\">σελάνα, σελάννα</span>) fr. <span class=\"gk\">Σελάς-να</span>, cf. <span class=\"gk\">σέλας</span>.)</div></div>"}